vated for its fruit (the peppercorn), which is usually dried and used as a spice and seasoning. The fruit is a drupe (stonefruit) which is about 5 mm (1⁄4 in) in diameter (fresh and fully mature), dark red, and contains a stone which encloses a single pepper seed. Peppercorns and the ground pepper derived from them may be described simply as pepper, or more precisely as black pepper (cooked and dried unripe fruit), green pepper (dried unripe fruit), or white pepper (ripe fruit seeds)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-peppercorn"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peppercorn"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":24,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Botok","dish/botok"],["Kerak telor","dish/kerak-telor"],["Mie aceh","dish/mie-aceh"],["Mie ayam","dish/mie-ayam"],["Rawon","dish/rawon"],["Sate padang","dish/sate-padang"],["Semur (Indonesian stew)","dish/semur-indonesian-stew"]]],["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Steak tartare","dish/steak-tartare"]]],["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Guanciale","dish/guanciale"]]],["Portuguese cuisine","cuisine/portuguese-cuisine",[["Amêijoas à Bulhão Pato","dish/ameijoas-a-bulhao-pato"],["Pataniscas","dish/pataniscas"]]],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine",[["Goulash","dish/goulash"],["Pelmeni","dish/pelmeni"]]],["Acehnese cuisine","cuisine/acehnese-cuisine",[["Mie aceh","dish/mie-aceh"]]],["Belgian cuisine","cuisine/belgian-cuisine",[["Steak tartare","dish/steak-tartare"]]],["Czech cuisine","cuisine/czech-cuisine",[["Steak tartare","dish/steak-tartare"]]],["Danish cuisine","cuisine/danish-cuisine",[["Æbleflæsk","dish/blefl-sk"]]],["Dutch cuisine","cuisine/dutch-cuisine",[["Pepernoot","dish/pepernoot"]]],["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine",[["Steak tartare","dish/steak-tartare"]]],["Greek cuisine","cuisine/greek-cuisine",[["Spanakorizo