sh/arrosticini","n":"Arrosticini","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Abruzzese and Molisan cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Arrosticini is a class of traditional dishes of skewered grilled meat characteristic of Abruzzo cuisine. They are typically made from mutton or lamb cut in chunks and pierced by a skewer. Arrosticini are cooked on a brazier with a typically elongated shape, called furnacella, which resembles a gutter. It is listed as a prodotto agroalimentare tradizionale (PAT) by the Italian Ministry of Agricultural, Food and Forestry Policies."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-arrosticini"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrosticini"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Abruzzese and Molisan cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-abruzzo"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Great Italian Chefs: Abruzzese recipes","ref":"site/greatitalianchefs-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"greatitalianchefs.com","note":"Collection of dishes from Abruzzo by Italian chefs on an established recipe site.","url":"https://www.greatitalianchefs.com/collections/abruzzese-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"site"},{"name":"The Pasta Project: Abruzzo","ref":"site/the-pasta-project-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"the-pasta-project.com","note":"Italy-based pasta blog's section on regional pasta dishes from Abruzzo.","url":"https://www.the-pasta-project.com/abruzzo/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Abruzzese and Molisan cuisine","links":[["Aurum (liqueur)","dish/aurum-liqueur"],["Brodetto alla vastese","dish/brodetto-alla-vastese"],["Centerbe","dish/centerbe"],["Confetti di Sulmona","dish/confetti-di-sulmona"],["Fiadone","dish/fiadone"],["Mortadella di Campotosto","dish/mortadella-di-campotosto"],["Pecora alla callara","dish/pecora-alla-callara"],["Torrone Nurzia","dish/torrone-nurzia"],["Vino cotto","dish/vino-cotto"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/d8/Campo_Imperatore_2009_-Ristoro_Mucciante_Arrosticini-_by_RaBoe_014.jpg/500px-Campo_Imperatore_2009_-Ristoro_Mucciante_Arrosticini-_by_RaBoe_014.jpg","w":500,"h":668,"by":"Ra Boe","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Campo_Imperatore_2009_-Ristoro_Mucciante_Arrosticini-_by_RaBoe_014.jpg"}},"ingredient/elettaria-cardamomum":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/elettaria-cardamomum","n":"Elettaria cardamomum","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Elettaria cardamomum, commonly known as green cardamom or true cardamom, is a herbaceous, perennial plant in the ginger family, native to southern India. It is the most common of the species whose seeds are used as a spice called cardamom that has a strong aroma used in both savory and sweet cooking. It is cultivated widely in tropical regions and reportedly naturalized in Réunion, Indochina, and Costa Rica."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-elettaria-cardamomum"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elettaria_cardamomum"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Moroccan cuisine","cuisine/moroccan-cuisine",[["Babbouche","dish/babbouche"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Anise","ingredient/anise"],["Liquorice","ingredient/liquorice"],["Mentha pulegium","ingredient/mentha-pulegium"],["Ras el hanout","ingredient/ras-el-hanout"],["Snail","ingredient/snail"],["Thymus","ingredient/thymus"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/f/f4/Elettaria_cardamomum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-057.jpg","w":500,"h":647,"by":"Franz Eugen Köhler, Köhler's Medizinal-Pflanzen","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elettaria_cardamomum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-057.jpg"}},"ingredient