d in Latin American cuisine, Philippine cuisine and in other areas that have received immigration from Spanish- and Portuguese-speaking countries, especially in France and the Southwestern United States."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-churro"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Churro"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Choux pastry","ingredient/choux-pastry"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Spain on a Fork","ref":"site/spainonafork-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"spainonafork.com","note":"Albert Bevia's video channel and site of traditional and everyday Spanish recipes.","url":"https://spainonafork.com/welcome2/","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"}]},{"h":"More from Spanish cuisine","links":[["Andrajos","dish/andrajos"],["Ataula","dish/ataula"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Buñuelo","dish/bunuelo"],["Caldo galego","dish/caldo-galego"],["Chistorra","dish/chistorra"],["Cocido","dish/cocido"],["Cuajada","dish/cuajada"],["El Quijote (restaurant)","dish/el-quijote-restaurant"],["El Willy","dish/el-willy"],["Embutido","dish/embutido"],["Esquina Común","dish/esquina-comun"],["Gazpacho","dish/gazpacho"],["Hojuela","dish/hojuela"],["Jamón","dish/jamon"],["Migas","dish/migas"],["Mojo (sauce)","dish/mojo-sauce"],["Ogasawara-Hakushaku-Tei","dish/ogasawara-hakushaku-tei"],["Patatas a lo pobre","dish/patatas-a-lo-pobre"],["Patatas bravas","dish/patatas-bravas"],["Picatostes","dish/picatostes"],["Pincho","dish/pincho"],["Pottage","dish/pottage"],["Salchichón","dish/salchichon"],["Salmorejo","dish/salmorejo"],["Sobrassada","dish/sobrassada"],["Soldaditos de Pavía","dish/soldaditos-de-pavia"],["Somni","dish/somni"],["Sopa de gato","dish/sopa-de-gato"],["Spanish omelette","dish/spanish-omelette"],["Spanish restaurant","dish/spanish-restaurant"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"],["Tapas","dish/tapas"],["Toro Bravo (restaurant)","dish/toro-bravo-restaurant"],["Turrón","dish/turron"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/4/42/Churros_en_vasos_en_Londres_-_A_Taste_of_Spain.jpg/500px-Churros_en_vasos_en_Londres_-_A_Taste_of_Spain.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Garry Knight from London, England","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Churros_en_vasos_en_Londres_-_A_Taste_of_Spain.jpg"}},"ingredient/pandanus":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/pandanus","n":"Pandanus","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 4 dishes across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Pandanus is a genus of monocots with about 578 accepted species. They are palm-like, dioecious trees and shrubs native to the Old World tropics and subtropics. Common names include pandan, screw palm and screw pine. The genus is classified in the order Pandanales, family Pandanaceae, and is the largest in the family."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-pandanus"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pandanus"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Kolak (food)","dish/kolak-food"],["Kue ape","dish/kue-ape"],["Nagasari","dish/nagasari"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"],["Palm sugar","ingredient/palm-sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Banana","ingredient/banana"],["Brown sugar","ingredient/brown-sugar"],["Pandan","ingredient/pandan"],["Sweet potato","ingredient/sweet-potato"],["Baking powder","ingredient/baking-powder"],["Banana leaf","ingredient/banana-leaf"],["Cooking banana","ingredient/cooking-banana"],["Rice flour","ingredient/rice-flour"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/69/Pandanus_utilis_fruit.JPG/500px-Pandanus_utilis_fruit.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"B.navez","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pandanus_utilis_fruit.JPG"}},"ingredient/dried-lime":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/dried-lime","n":"Dried lime","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Dried lime, also known as black lime, noomi basra (Iraq), limoo amani (Iran), and loomi (Oman), is a lime that has lost its water content, usually after having spent a majority of its drying time in the sun. They are used whole, sliced, or ground as a spice in Middle Eastern cuisine. Originating in the Persian Gulf – hence the Iranian name limoo amani and the Iraqi name noomi basra ('lemon from Basra') – dried limes are popular in cooking across the Middle East."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-dried-lime"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dried_lime"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Jewish cuisine","cuisine/jewish-cuisine",[["Gondi (food)","dish/gondi-food"]]],["Mizrahi Jewish cuisine","cuisine/mizrahi-jewish-cuisine",[["Gondi (food)","dish/gondi-food"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Besan","ingredient/besan"],["Cardamom","ingredient/cardamom"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Chickpea flour","ingredient/chickpea-flour"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Ground turkey","ingredient/ground-turkey"],["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"],["Meatball","ingredient/meatball"],["Onions","ingredient/onions"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/7/71/Loomi_at_market_in_Bahrain.JPG/500px-Loomi_at_market_in_Bahrain.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Theinfo","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Loomi_at_market_in_Bahrain.JPG"}},"dish/horcher-r