p-pearls"],["Eintopf","dish/eintopf"],["Flammekueche","dish/flammekueche"],["Gugelhupf","dish/gugelhupf"],["Hamburg steak","dish/hamburg-steak"],["Hedgehog slice","dish/hedgehog-slice"],["Herman ze German","dish/herman-ze-german"],["Kringle","dish/kringle"],["Labskaus","dish/labskaus"],["Landjäger","dish/landjager"],["Leberkäse","dish/leberkase"],["Mett","dish/mett"],["Mock turtle soup","dish/mock-turtle-soup"],["Potato pancake","dish/potato-pancake"],["Potato salad","dish/potato-salad"],["Rhein Haus Seattle","dish/rhein-haus-seattle"],["Rødgrød","dish/r-dgr-d"],["Sauerkraut","dish/sauerkraut"],["Spaghettieis","dish/spaghettieis"],["Speckkuchen","dish/speckkuchen"],["Spundekäs","dish/spundekas"],["Steckerlfisch","dish/steckerlfisch"],["Stippgrütze","dish/stippgrutze"],["Stollen","dish/stollen"],["Streuselkuchen","dish/streuselkuchen"],["Strudel","dish/strudel"],["The Student Prince (restaurant)","dish/the-student-prince-restaurant"],["Westfälische Rinderwurst","dish/westfalische-rinderwurst"],["Zopf","dish/zopf"],["Zum Zum","dish/zum-zum"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/e5/Horcher_-_Madrid.JPG/500px-Horcher_-_Madrid.JPG","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Tamorlan","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Horcher_-_Madrid.JPG"}},"dish/kadyos-manok-kag-ubad":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kadyos-manok-kag-ubad","n":"Kadyos, manok, kag ubad","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 3 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Kadyos, manok, kag ubad, commonly shortened to KMU, is a Filipino chicken soup or stew originating from the Hiligaynon people of the Western Visayas islands. The name of the dish means \"pigeon peas, chicken, and banana pith\"; the three main ingredients. It is similar to another Hiligayon dish, Kadyos, baboy, kag langka (\"KBL\"), except that it does not use a souring agent, and it uses chicken and banana pith (ubad, not to be confused with ubod which is heart of palm) instead. Like KBL, KMU is also characteristically purple in color due to the use of pigeon peas. Other ingredients include onions, lemongrass, thinly sliced ginger, siling haba pepper, and salt and pepper."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kadyos-manok-kag-ubad"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kadyos%2C_manok%2C_kag_ubad"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Filipino cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine"],["Mindanao cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-mindanao"],["Visayan cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-visayas"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Banana pith","ingredient/banana-pith"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Garcinia binucao","ingredient/garcinia-binucao"],["Pigeon pea","ingredient/pigeon-pea"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Panlasang Pinoy","ref":"site/panlasangpinoy-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"panlasangpinoy.com","note":"Vanjo Merano's large library of Filipino recipes and cooking videos.","url":"https://panlasangpinoy.com/filipino-food/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Kawaling Pinoy","ref":"site/kawalingpinoy-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"kawalingpinoy.com","note":"Lalaine Manalo's blog of Filipino home cooking.","url":"https://www.kawalingpinoy.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Flavours of Iloilo","ref":"site/flavoursofiloilo-blogspot-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"flavoursofiloilo.blogspot.com","note":"Blog of Ilonggo home dishes from Iloilo in the Western Visayas.","url":"https://flavoursofiloilo.blogspot.com/2013/05/how-about-some-chicken-binakol.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Filipino cuisine","links":[["Adobo (Filipino dish)","dish/adobo-filipino-dish"],["Aparon","dish/aparon"],["Banana ketchup","dish/banana-ketchup"],["Champorado","dish/champorado"],["Classic Savory","dish/classic-savory"],["Filipino barbecue","dish/filipino-barbecue"],["Food for the gods","dish/food-for-the-gods"],["Isaw","dish/isaw"],["Kadyos, baboy, kag langka","dish/kadyos-baboy-kag-langka"],["Kumukunsi","dish/kumukunsi"],["Mango float","dish/mango-float"],["Palapa (condiment)","dish/palapa-condiment"],["Pastil","dish/pastil"],["Piaparan","dish/piaparan"],["Pilipit","dish/pilipit"],["Piyanggang manok","dish/piyanggang-manok"],["Sushi bake","dish/sushi-bake"],["Tortang talong","dish/tortang-talong"]]}]},"dish/kavurma":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kavurma","n":"Kavurma","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Turkish cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Kavurma is a broad type of fried or sautéed meat dish found in Turkish cuisine. The name also refers to canned or preserved versions of a similar dish, prepared by dry frying the meat to render down the fat. It is present in cultures and cuisines of Turkey and neighbouring countries, including the Balkans, most notably in Bulgaria. Similar dishes are known in Central Asia as kuurdak, and in Hungary as tokány."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kavurma"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kavurma"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Ozlem's Turkish Table","ref":"site/ozlemsturkishtable-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"ozlemsturkishtable.com","note":"Turkish-born cook and teacher Ozlem Warren's blog of home-style Turkish recipes.","url":"https://ozlemsturkishtable.com/tag/turkish-recipes/page/9","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Turkish cuisine","links":[["Adana kebabı","dish/adana-kebab"],["Baba ghanoush","dish/baba-ghanoush"],["Bici bici","dish/bici-bici"],["Boortsog","dish/boortsog"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Çiğ köfte","dish/cig-kofte"],["Çökertme kebabı","dish/cokertme-kebab"],["Dede (restaurant)","dish/dede-restaurant"],["Doner kebab","dish/doner-kebab"],["Düğün çorbası","dish/dugun-corbas"],["Eggplant jam","dish/eggplant-